    "summary_one_sentence": "Six-year-old Willa sees her Surabaya alleyway as a magical paradise until her best friend suffers an accident and her playmates leave for school, forcing her to navigate a shifting, lonelier world.",
    "summary_short": "In a vibrant alley in Surabaya, six-year-old Willa lives a joyous life filled with imagination and daily adventures alongside her neighborhood friends. Her idyllic worldview faces its first real disruption when her closest companion suffers an accident, followed closely by her other playmates entering formal schooling. Left behind during the daytime, Willa must confront unfamiliar feelings of isolation as the comfort of her early childhood evolves. Ultimately, she learns to process these quiet transitions while holding onto the wonder of her changing environment.",
    "summary_long": "Six-year-old Willa spends her days exploring every nook and cranny of her small alley neighborhood in Surabaya, viewing her modest surroundings through a lens of boundless enchantment. Surrounded by a close-knit group of playmates, her life is a daily tapestry of creative games and effortless laughter. Everything feels permanent and perfect until a sudden accident injures her best friend, casting a temporary shadow over their usual antics. Shortly after, another subtle shift occurs as her friends, one after another, reach school age and begin attending daily classes. Suddenly, the once-bustling alleyway grows quiet during the day, leaving Willa with hours of unstructured time and a growing sense of solitude. As she observes her friends growing up and adopting new routines, Willa grapples with the confusion and bittersweet nature of childhood transitions. Her family and remaining community interactions help anchor her as she adjusts to the quiet space between early childhood and growing older. Through small moments of self-discovery, Willa slowly finds new ways to connect with her evolving world. By the end, she learns that while her childhood alley may be changing, its magic can endure inside her as she takes her own steps toward growing up.",
    "synopsis": "Set in a lively neighborhood alley in Surabaya, Indonesia, this gentle family drama centers on Willa, a imaginative six-year-old girl who views her immediate surroundings as a boundless playground. Her carefree routines are anchor points in a small world shared with a group of constant playmates. However, as her best friend experiences an unexpected accident and her peers begin enrolling in formal school, Willa's everyday reality begins to quiet down. Faced with the inevitable shifts of growing up and the solitude of quiet afternoons, Willa embarks on an emotional journey exploring change, friendship, and resilience.",
